items.a:
- [[g:Virtual Threads]] became final: thread-per-request code can handle much higher I/O concurrency without a large platform-thread pool.
- [[g:Pattern matching for `switch`]] and record patterns make closed data models concise and type-safe.
- Sequenced Collections standardize first/last/reversed operations.
- Generational ZGC became available; Structured Concurrency and Scoped Values were still preview APIs in Java 21.

**An exhaustive Java 21 `switch` must cover every guarded case:**

<pre><code><span class="k">sealed interface</span> Event <span class="k">permits</span> Refund, Charge {}
<span class="k">record</span> Refund(String id, <span class="k">long</span> amountCents) <span class="k">implements</span> Event {}
<span class="k">record</span> Charge(String id, <span class="k">long</span> amountCents) <span class="k">implements</span> Event {}
<span class="c">    </span>
<span class="k">switch</span> (event) {
    <span class="k">case</span> Refund(<span class="k">var</span> id, <span class="k">var</span> amount) <span class="k">when</span> amount &gt; <span class="n">0</span> -&gt; <span class="f">refund</span>(id, amount);
    <span class="k">case</span> Refund(<span class="k">var</span> id, <span class="k">var</span> amount)                 -&gt; <span class="k">throw new</span> IllegalArgumentException(<span class="s">"amount"</span>);
    <span class="k">case</span> Charge c                                      -&gt; <span class="f">charge</span>(c);
    <span class="k">case null</span>                                          -&gt; <span class="k">throw new</span> IllegalArgumentException(<span class="s">"event"</span>);
}</code></pre>

:::deep
The migration value is larger than a feature checklist:

- Virtual threads let blocking JDBC/HTTP code scale without callback conversion, but CPU-bound work still needs bounded parallelism and downstream capacity remains finite.
- On JDK 21–23, blocking under `synchronized` could pin a carrier. JDK 24 removed monitor-related pinning, so audit by target runtime rather than applying that workaround forever.
- Record patterns plus a sealed hierarchy allow compile-time exhaustiveness. A guarded pattern covers only values satisfying its guard; the second `Refund` arm above is required.
- Scoped Values became final in JDK 25; Structured Concurrency remains preview in JDK 25. Keep preview APIs behind a deliberate build/runtime flag and expect source migration.

For a Spring Boot blocking service, enabling virtual threads can be a small configuration change, but capacity tests must still cover DB connections, partner quotas, queue depth, deadlines, and memory per waiting request.
:::
